    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d207">

                <pb facs="0238" n="224" xml:id="pg224"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">811.003 Wallace, Henry A./45: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in China</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Gauss</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Chungking</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-04-21T15:00:00+07:00">April 21, 1944—3
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received April 21—1:13 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>695. Message from Mr. Wallace to Mme. Chiang has been delivered (your 521, April
                    18). Please inform Mr. Wallace that I shall be delighted to have him as my guest
                    for first evening and shall follow his wishes that evening not become a social
                    event but be spent with staff only.</p>
                <p>When place of Mr. Wallace’s first arrival in China becomes known Government will
                    probably as usual send representative, likely Hollington Tong,<anchor n="26"
                        xml:id="d207-f1"/> to join him there. I shall at same time send officer or
                    Attaché of Embassy. I assume Department will inform Mr. Wallace in outline of
                    present conditions in China before his departure.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Gauss</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d207-f1" n="26" xml:id="d207-f1-content">
                <p>Chinese Vice Minister of Information.</p>
            </note>
